  <tr><td>Audit log &amp; Undo rollback</td><td style='text-align:center;' class='no'>&#10007; No</td><td style='text-align:center;' class='ok'>&#10003; Yes</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>3.4 Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h4>Q1: I can see some days are greyed out and I cannot click on them. Why?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Those days are outside your allowed editing window (configured by Admin). Depending on your setting, you may only edit the current month up to today, or only the last N days. Contact your HR administrator if you believe your window needs to be extended.</p>

<h4>Q2: I tried to change an attendance value and the system asked me for a reason. What should I write?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Provide a clear and factual reason. For example: <em>&ldquo;Employee was marked Present by mistake. They were on authorized leave per supervisor approval.&rdquo;</em> or <em>&ldquo;Correcting typo &mdash; employee was marked Absent but was present.&rdquo;</em> This reason is stored in the audit log and can be reviewed by Admin.</p>

<h4>Q3: Why is Saturday showing as Auto Sat-Cut when the employee came on Friday and Monday?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> The system checks ALL 5 weekdays (Monday through Friday) of that week &mdash; not just Friday and Monday. If the employee was absent on any weekday (Tuesday, Wednesday, or Thursday), the Saturday is cut. Check the mid-week days for that employee. If the absence was genuinely covered (e.g., Paid Leave), it should not trigger a cut.</p>

<h4>Q4: An employee took a half-day in July and another in August. Will they be paired?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Yes. The system tracks half-days chronologically across the <strong>entire contract stint</strong> with no month boundary restriction. The July half-day (Carried) will automatically pair with the August half-day when August attendance is saved. You will be prompted to choose Paid or Unpaid pairing at that time.</p>

<h4>Q5: What is the difference between Present Days and Final Days in the Ledger?</h4>
<p><strong>A (for POC):</strong> <strong>Present Days</strong> is the computed sum from attendance, including any Global Adjustment added by Admin. <strong>Final Days</strong> is the same as Present Days unless Admin has specifically overridden it for a particular employee (e.g., to add or remove days for a reason not captured in the grid). For payroll and certificates, Final Days is the number used.</p>

<h4>Q6: I need Admin to fix a past attendance date that is locked for me. How do I request this?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Go to <strong>Remarks</strong> (from your dashboard or navigation). Click New Remark, select the radio button <strong>&ldquo;Attendance correction / changes&rdquo;</strong>, choose the employee, select the date, and clearly describe what needs to be changed and why. Click Send. The Admin will receive a notification and can make the correction directly on the locked date.</p>

<h4>Q7: What happens if a 2-year contract expires? Do workers disappear from the system?</h4>
<p><strong>A:</strong> No. When a contract period expires, the system automatically closes it and transitions all enrolled workers to &lsquo;ContractEnded&rsquo; status. Their historical attendance, leave, and wage records are sealed and preserved. To re-engage the same workers, the Admin creates a new contract period and uses <strong>Rejoin Employee</strong> to re-enroll them, preserving all prior history.</p>

<h4>Q8: I accidentally upgraded a worker to the wrong skill category. How do I undo it?</h4>
<p><strong>A (Admin):</strong> Go to <strong>Settings</strong> and open the <strong>Recent Employee Transitions Log</strong>. Locate the incorrect transition and click <strong>Undo Transaction</strong>. The system will automatically revert the category, close the incorrect engagement, and restore the prior one.</p>

